<title>FINLAND: TAMRO PROPOSES STAFF INCENTIVE PROGRAMME.</title>
<headline>TAMRO PROPOSES STAFF INCENTIVE PROGRAMME.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish pharma distributor Oy Tamro Ab said in a statement on Tuesday it had proposed to its annual general meeting an incentive programme involving non-interest bearing bonds with warrants for all staff.</p>
<p>&quot;Tamro's share capital can be increased by 5,000,000 new shares, i.e. FIM 50,000,000, as a result of subscriptions,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>It said it would issue up to 5,000 bonds with a 1,000 markka face value at par. The bonds would mature on May 30, 2000.</p>
<p>Each bond will carry warrants for 1,000 shares, of which 500 shall be marked A warrants and 500 B warrants, it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom, +358-9-680 50 240, news@reuters.fi</p>
